  "chapter": 650,
  "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
  "text": " \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 54 Chapter 650\n \n       MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 5162-A, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to amend the social services law, in relation to requiring\n        local social  services  districts  to  offer  to  pay  childcare\n        providers  via  a  direct  deposit for any subsidized child care\n        funds owed\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This bill would amend the social services law to  allow  local  social\nservice  districts to offer to pay child care providers subsidized funds\nvia direct deposit. Under the current system, a provider  has  to  wait,\nsometimes  more  than  four weeks, after submitting documentation to the\ncounty to get paid for care provided to children in their program.\n \n  Additionally, many of the providers who  receive  subsidy  funds  from\nlocal  social  services  districts  live  in communities that are tradi-\ntionally underserved by banks. The lack of access  to  financial  insti-\ntutions  creates a burden for these individuals to deposit their checks.\nThis bill helps individuals avoid other entities that they may turn  to,\nsuch as check cashing centers that charge higher rates and fees. Lastly,\nthis  legislation will create savings for local social service districts\nby eliminating the need to issue paper checks and  the  time  associated\nwith such tasks.\n \n  This  bill will create a more streamlined subsidy reimbursement system\nfor both child care providers and the  local  districts  and  any  costs\nrelated  to  potential  systems changes would be managed within existing\nagency resources. On that basis, I am pleased to sign this bill.\n \n  This bill is approved.                         (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                                ______\n",
